WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:03.533
Open the Cluster Storage Standard workflow after deployment.

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:08.099
It runs separately and is not inserted automatically into a recovery pipeline.

00:00:08.149 --> 00:00:12.536
Supply exactly three distinct replacement-container names and the settings intended

00:00:12.587 --> 00:00:16.470
for this cluster. Use a saved PE credential reference and trusted

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.761
HTTPS; never put its password in YAML.

00:00:19.925 --> 00:00:22.419
Select Discover default, read-only.

00:00:22.624 --> 00:00:26.670
Review the cluster UUID and the exact default-container name

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.784
and UUID captured into the configuration.

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.760
The numeric suffix matters.

00:00:31.952 --> 00:00:36.603
Multiple candidates, unsupported inventories or an unexpected default name block

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:40.406
review; the workflow does not guess which container can be removed.

00:00:40.656 --> 00:00:45.073
Review the replacements, settings and dependencies before requesting approval.

00:00:45.239 --> 00:00:49.477
A different administrator must approve the exact YAML and filename.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:52.271
Editing the file invalidates that approval.

00:00:52.407 --> 00:00:55.791
The operator confirmation binds submission to the reviewed cluster;

00:00:55.863 --> 00:00:58.965
a browser disconnect is not a reason to submit again.

00:00:59.262 --> 00:01:03.870
The worker verifies existing replacements before creating missing ones, then reads

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:07.297
back all three and checks the explicitly requested properties.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:11.296
Existing mismatches fail rather than being silently rewritten.

00:01:11.485 --> 00:01:15.871
Only the exact reviewed default is considered for cleanup, and dependencies must

00:01:15.879 --> 00:01:17.351
pass the conservative checks.

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:21.845
Retain the job and inspect actual storage state if creation, verification

00:01:22.109 --> 00:01:26.558
or cleanup fails. A familiar name does not prove a container is empty

00:01:26.609 --> 00:01:30.953
or disposable. Complete the documented storage and workload acceptance before

00:01:31.046 --> 00:01:32.916
using the result operationally.

00:01:33.222 --> 00:01:36.742
This walkthrough uses simulated inventory and deletes nothing.
